  What the non-overlapped system actually achieves per transform. The two
  memory banks ping-pong between FFT stages, so they cannot also
  double-buffer input against compute; overlapping the two would need a
  third bank.

HOW THE DERIVED COLUMNS ARE COMPUTED
  Throughput (transforms/s)      = maximum frequency / cycles per transform
  Energy per transform (nJ)      = dynamic power x cycles x clock period
  Throughput per watt (transf/J) = 1 / energy per transform. These are the
                                   same quantity: transforms per second
                                   divided by joules per second is
                                   transforms per joule. It is not a
                                   separate measurement.
  Throughput per 1000 logic LUTs = throughput / (logic LUTs / 1000)

